// Title: Scheduled Task Executing Encoded Payload from Registry
// ID: c4eeeeae-89f4-43a7-8b48-8d1bdfa66c78
// Status: test
// Level: high
// Author: pH-T (Nextron Systems), @Kostastsale, TheDFIRReport, X__Junior (Nextron Systems), Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-02-12
// Tags: attack.privilege-escalation, attack.execution, attack.persistence, attack.t1053.005, attack.t1059.001
// Description: Detects the creation of a schtask that potentially executes a base64 encoded payload stored in the Windows Registry using PowerShell.
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

process where ((process.command_line like "*_/Create*") and ((process.command_line like "*_FromBase64String*" or process.command_line like "*_encodedcommand*")) and ((process.command_line like "*_Get-ItemProperty*" or process.command_line like "*_ gp *")) and ((process.command_line like "*_HKCU:*" or process.command_line like "*_HKLM:*" or process.command_line like "*_registry::*" or process.command_line like "*_HKEY_*")) and ((process.executable endswith "\\schtasks.exe") or (process.pe.original_file_name == "schtasks.exe")))
